  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "How many ways can you arrange the letters in the word MISSISSIPPI so that the first or last letter is S?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$21\\,420$ arrangements.\n\nAdd the counts with S first and S last, then subtract the count with S at both ends.",
      "worked": "There are four I's, four S's, two P's and one M. Let $A$ contain arrangements with S first and $B$ contain arrangements with S last. Fixing one S leaves ten letters; fixing both ends leaves nine letters.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|A|&=\\frac{10!}{4!\\,3!\\,2!}=12\\,600\\\\|B|&=\\frac{10!}{4!\\,3!\\,2!}=12\\,600\\\\|A\\cap B|&=\\frac{9!}{4!\\,2!\\,2!}=3\\,780\\\\|A\\cup B|&=|A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|\\\\|A\\cup B|&=12\\,600+12\\,600-3\\,780\\\\|A\\cup B|&=21\\,420\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
